G='Science, invention & culture'
E=[
("First telephone call",1876,"10 March 1876","Invention","Boston, USA","Birth of telecommunications","Alexander Graham Bell spoke the first words over a telephone to his assistant: 'Mr Watson, come here, I want to see you.'","Three days earlier Bell had received his patent, filed hours before Elisha Gray's caveat. Bell's transmitter in this test used a liquid (acid water) design similar to Gray's, fuelling claims that he had seen Gray's papers. Bell demonstrated the phone at the 1876 Centennial Exhibition, where Emperor Pedro II of Brazil exclaimed 'My God, it talks!'. By 1886 over 150,000 Americans had phones.","Invention_of_the_telephone","Americas"),
("Edison's light and Pearl Street station",1882,"1879–1882","Invention","New York, USA","Start of electric utilities","Edison's team demonstrated long-lasting light bulbs at Menlo Park on New Year's Eve 1879, and opened the Pearl Street power station in 1882.","Pearl Street, in Manhattan's financial district, supplied direct current to 82 customers and 400 lamps at first, including the New York Times and J. P. Morgan's offices. DC could only travel about a mile, limiting the system. Swan's competing bulbs lit London's Savoy Theatre in 1881.","Pearl_Street_Station","Americas"),
("Niagara Falls power plant",1895,"1895–1896","Invention","USA","Victory of alternating current","The Adams Power Plant at Niagara Falls began generating AC electricity using Tesla's polyphase system.","In 1896 power was sent 42 km to Buffalo, proving long-distance AC transmission. It ended the 'war of the currents', and Tesla's statue now stands at Niagara Falls on both the US and Canadian sides.","Adams_Power_Plant_Transformer_House","Americas"),
("Lumière brothers' first film screening",1895,"28 December 1895","Cultural change","Paris, France","Birth of cinema","The Lumière brothers screened ten short films to a paying audience at the Grand Café in Paris.","The films included workers leaving their factory; a legend says audiences fled from a film of an arriving train. In July 1896 the Lumières' agents screened films at Watson's Hotel in Bombay, India's first cinema show. Within a decade nickelodeons spread across America.","Auguste_and_Louis_Lumi%C3%A8re","Europe"),
("Marconi's transatlantic radio signal",1901,"12 December 1901","Invention","Newfoundland and Cornwall","Wireless communication across oceans","Guglielmo Marconi received the Morse letter 'S' sent from Cornwall to St John's, Newfoundland.","Some scientists doubted it, since he used a kite antenna and noisy reception. His detector used a mercury coherer likely based on J. C. Bose's design. In 1912 wireless messages from the sinking Titanic saved 700 lives.","Guglielmo_Marconi","Global"),
("Discovery of penicillin",1928,"September 1928","Discovery","London, UK","Start of the antibiotic age","Alexander Fleming noticed mould killing bacteria in a petri dish at St Mary's Hospital.","Fleming's 1929 paper attracted little interest. In 1940 Florey and Chain showed penicillin cured infections in mice; mass production in the US enabled treating soldiers at D-Day. Before antibiotics, a scratch could kill.","Discovery_of_penicillin","Europe"),
("First television broadcasts",1936,"1926–1936","Cultural change","London","Mass broadcasting","John Logie Baird demonstrated television in 1926, and the BBC launched the world's first regular high-definition service in 1936.","The 1936 Berlin Olympics were broadcast in Germany as Nazi propaganda. Television spread rapidly after WWII; Doordarshan started in Delhi in 1959.","History_of_television","Europe"),
("Manhattan Project begins",1942,"1942","Science and war","USA","Race for the atomic bomb","The US launched a secret project to build an atomic bomb, after Einstein's 1939 letter warned of German research.","Under General Leslie Groves and J. Robert Oppenheimer, 130,000 people worked at Los Alamos, Oak Ridge and Hanford, most without knowing their purpose. Enrico Fermi achieved the first chain reaction in Chicago on 2 December 1942. Soviet spies infiltrated the project.","Manhattan_Project","Americas"),
("Trinity nuclear test",1945,"16 July 1945","Science and war","New Mexico, USA","The first nuclear explosion","The first atomic bomb, 'the Gadget', exploded in the desert with the force of about 25,000 tonnes of TNT.","The flash was seen 300 km away. Scientists had bet on whether it would ignite the atmosphere. Local residents, many Hispanic and Native American, were not warned and were exposed to fallout; they have never been fully compensated.","Trinity_(nuclear_test)","Americas"),
("Discovery of the DNA double helix",1953,"25 April 1953","Discovery","Cambridge, UK","Birth of molecular biology","Watson and Crick published the double helix model of DNA, based partly on Rosalind Franklin's X-ray data.","Their one-page paper noted that base pairing 'immediately suggests a possible copying mechanism'. Franklin's role was minimised for decades.","Molecular_Structure_of_Nucleic_Acids","Europe"),
("Sputnik launched",1957,"4 October 1957","Space","USSR","Start of the space age","The Soviet Union launched Sputnik 1, the first artificial satellite.","Its beeping signal shocked the US, leading to NASA's founding (1958), more science education funding and DARPA, which later created ARPANET. Laika, a stray dog, became the first animal in orbit on Sputnik 2 but died within hours.","Sputnik_1","Europe"),
("Yuri Gagarin orbits Earth",1961,"12 April 1961","Space","USSR","First human in space","Yuri Gagarin orbited Earth once in Vostok 1, in 108 minutes.","He ejected from the capsule and parachuted separately, a fact hidden for years because records required landing in the spacecraft. He died in a training jet crash in 1968.","Yuri_Gagarin","Europe"),
("India's first rocket launch from Thumba",1963,"21 November 1963","Space","Kerala, India","Birth of the Indian space programme","A US-made Nike-Apache sounding rocket launched from Thumba, near Thiruvananthapuram.","Rocket parts were carried on bicycles and a bullock cart, and a church served as the office. Vikram Sarabhai and young engineers like A. P. J. Abdul Kalam worked there; ISRO was founded in 1969.","Thumba_Equatorial_Rocket_Launching_Station","South Asia"),
("ARPANET's first message",1969,"29 October 1969","Invention","California, USA","Birth of the internet","Charley Kline at UCLA tried to type 'LOGIN' to Stanford; the system crashed after 'LO'.","The network grew to connect universities and military sites, and TCP/IP (1983) created the modern internet.","ARPANET","Americas"),
("Smiling Buddha nuclear test",1974,"18 May 1974","Science and war","Pokhran, Rajasthan","India becomes a nuclear power","India tested a nuclear device it called a 'peaceful nuclear explosion'.","The test, led by Raja Ramanna, led to the creation of the Nuclear Suppliers Group to restrict nuclear trade. In 1998 India conducted five more tests (Operation Shakti), followed by Pakistan.","Smiling_Buddha","South Asia"),
("Aryabhata satellite launched",1975,"19 April 1975","Space","USSR (for India)","India's first satellite","India's first satellite, named after the mathematician, was launched on a Soviet rocket.","Built by ISRO at Peenya, Bangalore, it was featured on the ₹2 note. India launched its own satellite with SLV-3 in 1980.","Aryabhata_(satellite)","South Asia"),
("Launch of the iPhone",2007,"9 January 2007","Invention","USA","Smartphone revolution","Steve Jobs unveiled the iPhone, combining a phone, internet and touchscreen.","The App Store (2008) created a new economy; Android spread cheaper smartphones worldwide, bringing internet access to billions in India and Africa.","IPhone_(1st_generation)","Americas"),
("Launch of UPI",2016,"11 April 2016","Invention","India","Digital payments revolution","The National Payments Corporation of India launched the Unified Payments Interface.","UPI processes billions of transactions a month, with India accounting for nearly half of the world's real-time digital payments.","Unified_Payments_Interface","South Asia"),
("Release of ChatGPT",2022,"30 November 2022","Invention","USA","Mass adoption of generative AI","OpenAI released ChatGPT, reaching 100 million users in two months.","It sparked a global race in large language models and debates about jobs, education and safety.","ChatGPT","Global"),
("Snowden revelations",2013,"June 2013","Revelation","Global","Exposed mass surveillance","Edward Snowden leaked NSA documents revealing global surveillance.","Programmes like PRISM collected data from internet companies, and allies' leaders' phones were tapped. Snowden fled to Russia.","Edward_Snowden","Global"),
]
